# Independent block projection implementation review

Target: 652d3b2, separate scratch workspace and target directory. Initial fixed code was four dirty files over a163764e93e2809f8013d7bbe16721082f979143; final delta source includes the capacity guard, stack marker, renderer identifier and specification. Nine delta copies match the final commit exactly; 493 present production/test/schema/fixture dependencies also match Git blobs. Production and manuscript files were not edited. The earlier design record is ../review-block-projection-design/manifest.json.

Reviewed the actual annotated block implementation against Doc spec05/21 and GFM table/list grammar. Table and flat-list branches retain the prior section_seen guard and reject adjacent List nodes. Only genuinely empty cell content is accepted; empty visible decorations, title/paragraph and InlineCode are not silently discarded. Headerless and zero-column tables are explicitly unsupported, while nonzero-column header-only tables and empty cells remain representable. Flat lists preserve start, checkbox Option and multiple Sentences within one Paragraph; empty/nested/multiple-block bodies remain rejected. Existing prepare/source/label/requirement validation remains prior to emission. No unresolved assets/foreign/relative links are fabricated.

Capacity finding: initial table_code checked usize addition but not isize allocation capacity. This was a static boundary finding, not a demonstrated huge-memory crash. Root added the isize guard with sticky AllocationLimit; the final source was checked. Root also replaced format/repeat allocations for list markers with a fixed 11-byte decimal buffer and constant indentation slice. Range 0..999999999 ensures every buffer index and slice bound; repeating the same marker avoids later-item numeric overflow. Table escaping adds exactly one backslash before each pipe and leaves existing code backslashes alone; delimiter padding and text/control checks still occur in the common code writer. No remaining blocker was found in these changes.

Independent native actual Doc -> GFM cases: all length-three strings from a/pipe/backslash/backtick/space that contain a pipe (61), each through direct Code, Strong(Code), Ruby reading Code and Anno note Code: 244 cases retain exact Code bytes and two table cells. Four ordered-start cases (0/9/10/999999999) retain two items, explicit checkbox state and a hard break at the proper marker width. Total 248 cases. The complete source and Markdown results before and after capacity/marker fixes are byte-identical.

Additional independent native boundaries: nine malformed/unrepresentable shapes reject with the intended projection error, including headerless/zero-column, empty Strong cell, decoration-hidden adjacent code, section-external list/table, mixed adjacent lists, U64MAX start and empty checked paragraph. A separate actual mixed list/table document passes full SyntaxBundle parsing/lowering, real CBOR encode/decode and a distinct empty receiving FoundationCodec. It renders with fresh SourceAdmission for each trial. SourceBytes0 and successUsage-1 Work/Allocation/Output/Nodes plus Depth0/cancel preserve the exact expected StopReason. Re-entry with the same stopped Budget changes no Usage. The original document remains equal. This yields 17 failure/first-receiver/budget observations. Managed annotated_blocks five tests were also independently executed successfully.

Probe correction retained: initial list test used literal `[x] plain`, which is malformed Doc annotation syntax. The fixture was corrected to explicit Sentence/Text without changing production. Initial source/log remain; the corrected public API probe passes. Initial WASI invocation occurred before the asynchronous build finished and reports missing module, not an executed test failure; its command/log are preserved separately from later execution.

Renderer /2 is shared by generated metadata and canonical registry. Existing chapter13 Git change is only the renderer identifier in its metadata; its prior body bytes remain unchanged. The ordinary restricted markdown() implementation was not widened. This review does not certify a canonical switch for chapters00/01 or any other page, nor general nested lists/headerless table support, aggregate migration acceptance or browser platform equivalence.

Native/WASI commands, executable hashes, outputs and final cross-target status are recorded separately in the evidence index. Scratch-only binaries/probes are outside production; target/workspace directories are not archive payloads. Refer to final-status.json for the completed execution counts and explicitly retained failed attempts.
